{
  "_comment": "Model ladders. Rungs top-down; opencode-go/* = OpenCode Go subscription, openrouter/* = OpenRouter, opencode-zen/* = zen free tier via the GCP relay (RETIRED: the relay VM's ephemeral IP moved, the URL is pinned to the old one, and zen-rings/* covers the same models — no rung uses it), zen-rings/* = zen free tier through the ring of GitHub Actions repos. NO ALIASES: one name, one ladder. Ladders: service (bot service calls, roles build/plan/explore/general/review + classify/summarize/format/route/gate), doctor (strong Go tier), research (hermes reads), conversation (hh-skill writing), build/build advanced/plan/explore/general/review (role ladders, #71), vision/vision advanced (images), free (hard $0 ceiling). ZEN-RINGS RETIRED (#329): opencode zen killed anonymous access — 'Bearer public' + the fingerprint headers get HTTP 429 FreeUsageLimitError from EVERY egress (residential, GHA Azure, CF colos), keys ignored. The quota is ~1000 req/model/day per clean FIXED IP until ~00:00 UTC; one relay IP yields pennies for our traffic, so the segment is gone from every ladder and 'zen_ring: false' switches the ring machinery (pool, relay, canary) off. Nothing is deleted: zen-rings/* rungs come back by config alone if opencode offers a usable path. NOTE: 'opencode-zen/*' (the retired GCP-relay ids) were already dead before.",
